<ProseLayout
  title="About — Font Finder Tool"
  description="Font Finder Tool helps designers and developers identify fonts from images and find free alternatives."
  heading="About Font Finder Tool"
>
  <p>Font Finder Tool started with a simple frustration: font identifiers tell you a name, then leave you to work out whether you can afford it, whether you’re allowed to use it, and what it actually looks like with your words.</p>
  <p>So we built a finder that goes the whole way. Every result is marked <strong>Free</strong> or <strong>Paid</strong>, previewed in your own text, and comes with a license summary and a direct link. When the exact font is commercial, we suggest free lookalikes you can use straight away.</p>

  <h2>How matching works</h2>
  <p>Images are matched by specialised font-recognition services and AI image analysis, then cross-checked against the open-source catalog from <a href="https://fontsource.org" rel="noopener">Fontsource</a> (which includes all of Google Fonts) to confirm which matches are free and how they’re licensed.</p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>Found a wrong match, or want a feature? Email <a href="mailto:hello@fontfindertool.com">hello@fontfindertool.com</a>.</p>
</ProseLayout>
